{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/138856-werewolf-with-less-spirit-world-more-real-world","id":138856,"title":"Werewolf with less spirit world, more real world","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-15T21:00:36-07:00","id":138856,"title":"Werewolf with less spirit world, more real world","content":"This is classified now","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3028,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","user":"viskarenvisla","date":".  Sealing content 03-06-2022, 03:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T22:30:09-07:00","id":138966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>viskarenvisla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/138856-werewolf-with-less-spirit-world-more-real-world#post138856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fighting spirits doesn't always feel very real or interesting, and I've noticed that the most compelling and interesting stories, and the chosen foe of most characters, is definitely Anshega wolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>When you fight spirits, you find personified constructs of the real word. A spirit of poverty, hanging over a fucked up neighborhood. A spirit of intolerance, infesting the community. The echo of a gruesome murder that happened only weeks ago. The spirit of your own weakness and fear.<br /> <br /> There is nothing that is cartoony or fantasy-like about that; and it's important to remember that spirits always come to being as a consequence of actions in the Flesh. Spirit encounters are never random. Remember that the Hisil is a place of meaning, spirituality and, quite literally, a Shadow of the Flesh. You don't get to face some anger spirit, you'll face the embodied wrath of a teenager about to go on a killing spree in his school. The murder spirit trying to rip your guts out is an idealized reflection of that serial killer who slaughtered a two digit number of people in the city decades ago. The lust spirit trying to seduce you - it's the PC's own repressed feelings of sexuality, trying desperately to find a release.<br /> <br /> Remember also that the best, most effective way to fight a spirit is to take away its essence source by evoking changes in the Flesh - Solve the murder case and bring the murder to justice. Stop the pollution. Conquer your fear. Anything else is just a temporary solution. Hunting spirits is very much about dealing with both worlds and hunting in both worlds - Shadow and Flesh - at the same time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>viskarenvisla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/138856-werewolf-with-less-spirit-world-more-real-world#post138856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone have any ideas for Werewolf the do away with the Spirit World or relegate it to a position of smaller importance?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Forsaken Chronicler's Guide, yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>viskarenvisla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/138856-werewolf-with-less-spirit-world-more-real-world#post138856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, does anyone think this is a good idea?</div> </div> </div> </div>Since you've asked - I don't think it's a good idea. Without the Shadow, the game loses much of what's interesting about the game to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T22:30:23-07:00","id":138968,"title":"","content":"n your place, I would use <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/wolf-blooded/\" target=\"_blank\">new Wolf Blooded </a>spoiled from <b>Idigam Chronicles</b> - as &quot;lesser werewolves&quot; they are great to omitting <i>Hisil </i>importance, on beginning at last. Myself, I made private <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/122016-quasi-idigam-chronicles-wolf-blooded#post135284\">fan version of WB</a> cause I couldn't wait at least to September. None the less I run now Flesh Wolf-Blooded group and it looks nice enough. Game resemblance very much movie <i>Wolf</i> with Jack Nicholson from 1994 in Swedish Lapland. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T23:06:18-07:00","id":139018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/138856-werewolf-with-less-spirit-world-more-real-world?p=138966#post138966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When you fight spirits, you find personified constructs of the real word. A spirit of poverty, hanging over a fucked up neighborhood. A spirit of intolerance, infesting the community. The echo of a gruesome murder that happened only weeks ago. The spirit of your own weakness and fear.<br /> <br /> There is nothing that is cartoony or fantasy-like about that; and it's important to remember that spirits always come to being as a consequence of actions in the Flesh. Spirit encounters are never random. Remember that the Hisil is a place of meaning, spirituality and, quite literally, a Shadow of the Flesh. You don't get to face some anger spirit, you'll face the embodied wrath of a teenager about to go on a killing spree in his school. The murder spirit trying to rip your guts out is an idealized reflection of that serial killer who slaughtered a two digit number of people in the city decades ago. The lust spirit trying to seduce you - it's the PC's own repressed feelings of sexuality, trying desperately to find a release.<br /> <br /> Remember also that the best, most effective way to fight a spirit is to take away its essence source by evoking changes in the Flesh - Solve the murder case and bring the murder to justice. Stop the pollution. Conquer your fear. Anything else is just a temporary solution. Hunting spirits is very much about dealing with both worlds and hunting in both worlds - Shadow and Flesh - at the same time.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Forsaken Chronicler's Guide, yes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Since you've asked - I don't think it's a good idea. Without the Shadow, the game loses much of what's interesting about the game to me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm glad you contributed, it helps me think about how to frame this and ask myself what could be put in the Shadow's place. The Hisil can be interesting but I envision a game that focuses less on the supernatural ephemera that exists outside of the Uratha and more of their internal struggles, their personal horror. Spirit Herding just seems like something that's very defeated from the essence of the Werewolf myths, which is more personified in terrible foes like The Anshega. I'm not a big fan of the backstory either, with some big wolf thundering around Pangaea being chased by his multicolored god-children.<br /> <br /> I prefer the psychological horror aspects of World of Darkness games. Wraith: The Oblivion was my favorite. I find that The Hisil, while it can be a way to confront the horror of the World of Darkness, distracts from actual looking inward. Your murder, your rage, your sins, they're not the insidious whispers of your conscience and your sanity crumbling under the pressure of The Wolf - they're terrifying rippy spirits that you have to fight or bind. Cool I guess, but it still feels forced. It's a good way to justify werewolves having magical powers but I think there are better ways to do that.<br /> <br /> Thanks for your thoughts and your reference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T23:19:30-07:00","id":139036,"title":"","content":"Have you ever played Silent Hill? It's one of the main inspirations of the Shadow. And it's ALL about internal horror. In the Shadow, werewolves face their internal demons. They face the internal demons of everyone in fact. And you're welcome!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T23:24:10-07:00","id":139037,"title":"","content":"(posting from my phone sorry about the formattin :-) )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T23:39:29-07:00","id":139044,"title":"","content":"I have indeed played Silent Hill - it's an awesome game and replete with wonderful imagery, especially in the second and third games. However I feel that those games fit in better with something else rather than Werewolf. The horror in Werewolf is something I'm aiming for to be more personal, more rooted in the real world and less mystic. What would be something that could replace gifts from spirits? I liked some of the Bestowments and Transmutations from Promethean. I know very little about systems besides Mage and Werewolf and Vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T06:48:29-07:00","id":139260,"title":"","content":"Not to derail, but if you loved <b>Wraith: the Oblivion</b> (fellow fan of that game here), and based on what you've said so far that you're looking for, maybe <b>Promethean: the Created</b> might be a better game choice for you to play? Promethean is, in many ways, the spiritual successor to Wraith. Lots of similar themes.<br /> <br /> If not interested, don't mind me.....carry on.....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T08:41:38-07:00","id":139360,"title":"","content":"It seems like everything has to involve the shadow, but it really doesn't. In the opener for Lodges it talks about a Storm Lord pack who can't access the shadow (mostly cause they screwed their territory into the ground and are afraid of it). They do alot of local things. &gt;.&gt; Granted their alpha is a pretty awful person and the pack can boast of causing at least one unihar...<br /> <br /> Also picked up the Werewolf the apocalypse storytellers blah blah blah books and they have some damn useful information in there. Hell on paragraph talks about hunts that wont involve the supernatural for weeks on end. If you want to go the wolf hunting route.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}